$post_body = <<<'HTML'
<p>Roller shades in natural textures and honeycomb shades in warm neutrals are the leading shade styles for 2026. Roman shades have also come back strongly after a quieter few years. The direction across all shade categories is toward organic materials, warmer tones, and softer looks.</p>
<p>Here's what's current, what's declining, and what's worth knowing if you're updating your window treatments in Aurora, IL this year.</p>
%IMAGE1%
<h2 id="roller-shades-in-natural-textures-are-the-most-ordered-shade">Roller Shades in Natural Textures Are the Most Ordered Shade in 2026</h2>
<p>Roller shades in linen textures, bamboo-look fabrics, and woven-effect materials are the most ordered single shade type in residential installs going into 2026. The clean, minimal profile when raised and the wide range of fabric options make them the most versatile shade product available.</p>
<p>The colors driving orders: warm white, oat, sand, greige, and natural linen. These replaced the cool whites and grays that led through the 2010s.</p>
<p>Our <a href="%BASE%/window-treatments/shades/roller-shades/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">roller shades</a> include natural-texture fabric options in the warm tones that are leading 2026 orders.</p>
<h2 id="roman-shades-are-growing-after-a-quieter-few-years">Roman Shades Are Growing After a Quieter Few Years</h2>
<p>Roman shades are back in significant demand in 2026. The broader return of natural materials and layered soft treatments has brought roman shades back as a go-to choice for kitchens, dining rooms, and reading areas.</p>
<p>The fold styles that are most current: flat fold and hobbled fold in solid natural fabrics rather than printed patterns. The direction is texture over pattern.</p>
<p>Our <a href="%BASE%/window-treatments/shades/roman-shades/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">roman shades</a> include solid and textured fabric options in the current styles.</p>
<h2 id="honeycomb-shades-in-earthy-tones-are-strong-in-2026">Honeycomb Shades in Earthy Tones Are Strong in 2026</h2>
<p>Honeycomb shades in warm sand, greige, and off-white are a top choice for bedrooms and energy-conscious homeowners in 2026. The energy insulation angle is growing as a selling point alongside the light control. In an Illinois climate with cold winters and humid summers, double-cell honeycomb shades have a real functional argument.</p>
<p>The color direction mirrors the broader shade market: warm neutrals over cool ones.</p>
<p>Our <a href="%BASE%/window-treatments/shades/honeycomb-shades/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">honeycomb shades</a> are available in single-cell and double-cell configurations with the current warm neutral color families.</p>
<h2 id="sheer-shades-are-popular-in-living-rooms-in-2026">Sheer Shades Are Popular in Living Rooms in 2026</h2>
<p>Sheer shades in neutral fabrics continue to be a strong choice for living rooms and front-facing rooms. They filter direct sunlight while maintaining a connection to the outdoors, and they layer well under heavier drapery panels when you want full coverage in the evening.</p>
<p>The look that's current: a simple sheer in a warm neutral with no decorative trim, paired with a heavier linen-look drapery panel.</p>
<p>Our <a href="%BASE%/window-treatments/shades/sheer-shades/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">sheer shades</a> are available in neutral fabric weights suited to the 2026 layered treatment approach.</p>
<h2 id="what-shade-styles-are-declining-in-2026">What Shade Styles Are Declining in 2026</h2>
<p>Bright white cellular shades in a single flat tone are declining. They were the dominant honeycomb shade look for years, but the shift toward warmer interiors has left them looking out of place in most rooms that have updated their palette.</p>
<p>Roller shades in cool gray and stark white are also declining. Blackout is still a popular functional choice, but the color direction has shifted even in blackout fabrics toward off-whites and warm tones.</p>
<p>Very narrow roller shades, particularly the kind installed in rented apartments and builder-grade homes, look dated in a remodeled space.</p>
%IMAGE2%
<h2 id="getting-2026-shade-styles-in-aurora-il">Getting 2026 Shade Styles in Aurora, IL</h2>
